IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `act-ch9-repeal-and-amendment`

-- Tests for act-ch9-repeal-and-amendment.l4.
-- Every expected value is read from the section named beside the assertion, and was written before the run.

§ `Tests: chapter 9, Repeal and amendment`

§§ `Part 9.1: General`

-- s 82: amend includes modify.
#ASSERT `s 82: the change is an amendment for chapter 9` `an amendment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 82: the change is an amendment for chapter 9` `a modification` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 82: the change is an amendment for chapter 9` `a repeal` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 82: law means an Act or statutory instrument.
#ASSERT `s 82: the kind of document is a law for chapter 9` `an Act`
#ASSERT `s 82: the kind of document is a law for chapter 9` `a commencement notice`
-- s 82: repeal includes lapse and expire.
#ASSERT `s 82: the change is a repeal for chapter 9` `a repeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 82: the change is a repeal for chapter 9` `a lapse` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 82: the change is a repeal for chapter 9` `an expiry` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 82: the change is a repeal for chapter 9` `an amendment` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 83 (1): if an Act amends a statutory instrument, the instrument may be amended or repealed as if the amendment had been made by another statutory instrument of that kind.
#ASSERT `s 83 (1): the instrument may be amended or repealed as if the amendment had been made by another statutory instrument of that kind` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 83 (1): the instrument may be amended or repealed as if the amendment had been made by another statutory instrument of that kind` FALSE)

-- s 84 (1) (a), (b), (c) and s 84 (3) (a), (b): repeal or amendment does not revive, affect previous operation, affect existing rights, affect proof, affect a right, privilege or liability provided for by the law.
#ASSERT `s 84 (1), (3): the repeal or amendment of a law affects the thing` `something not in force or existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect (revival)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 84 (1), (3): the repeal or amendment of a law affects the thing` `the previous operation of the law, or anything done, begun or suffered under it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 84 (1), (3): the repeal or amendment of a law affects the thing` `an existing right, privilege or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the law` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 84 (1), (3): the repeal or amendment of a law affects the thing` `the proof of anything that has happened` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 84 (1), (3): the repeal or amendment of a law affects the thing` `a right, privilege or liability saved by the law` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 84 (1), (3): the repeal or amendment of a law affects the thing` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 84 (2): an investigation, proceeding or remedy in relation to an existing right, privilege or liability may be started, exercised, continued or completed as if the repeal had not happened.
#ASSERT `s 84 (2): the investigation, proceeding or remedy may be started, exercised, continued or completed as if the repeal or amendment had not happened` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 84 (2): the investigation, proceeding or remedy may be started, exercised, continued or completed as if the repeal or amendment had not happened` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 84 (4): "This section does not limit any other provision of this chapter."
#ASSERT NOT (`s 84 (4): s 84 limits any other provision of this chapter`)

-- s 84A (1): an act or omission is only an offence if done or not done after the law commences; both sides of the commencement day (10 March 2026).
#ASSERT `s 84A (1): the act or omission is an offence` TRUE (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 84A (1): the act or omission is an offence` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 84A (1): the act or omission is an offence` TRUE (Date 11 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Where the law does not make the act an offence, the section does not answer.
#ASSERT `s 84A (1): the act or omission is an offence` FALSE (Date 11 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 84A (2): an increase in the penalty applies only to an offence committed after the law commences.
#ASSERT `s 84A (2): the increase in the penalty applies to the offence` (Date 11 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 84A (2): the increase in the penalty applies to the offence` (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026))
-- s 84A (3): a reduction applies to an offence committed before or after the law commences, but does not affect a penalty imposed before the law commences.
#ASSERT `s 84A (3): the reduction in the penalty applies to the offence` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 84A (3): the reduction in the penalty applies to the offence` TRUE)
-- s 84A (4): law means an Act or subordinate law.
#ASSERT `s 84A (4): the kind of document is a law for s 84A` `an Act`
#ASSERT `s 84A (4): the kind of document is a law for s 84A` `a subordinate law`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 84A (4): the kind of document is a law for s 84A` `a disallowable instrument`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 84A (4): the kind of document is a law for s 84A` `a statutory instrument of another kind`)

§§ `Part 9.2: Repeal`

-- s 85 (2), (3) are in the time module; s 85 (2) Note: under s 74 a law commences at the beginning of the day unless otherwise provided.
#ASSERT `s 85: when the repeal of a law takes effect` (Date 5 5 2026) TRUE (JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 5 5 2026))) EQUALS JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (Date 5 5 2026))

-- s 86 (1): the first law is not revived only because the other law is repealed.
#ASSERT `s 86 (1): the first law is revived` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 86 (1): the first law is revived` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 86 (2): the continuing operation of the amendments is not affected only because the other law is repealed.
#ASSERT `s 86 (2): the continuing operation of the amendments made by the other law is affected` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 86 (2): the continuing operation of the amendments made by the other law is affected` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`s 86 (3): s 86 limits any other provision of this chapter`)
-- s 86 (5): amended does not include modified.
#ASSERT `s 86 (5): the change is an amendment for s 86` `a modification` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 86 (5): the change is an amendment for s 86` `an amendment` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 86 (5): law includes a rule of the common law (including equity). Examples: a common law offence; a common law rule of practice or procedure; a right to equitable relief.
#ASSERT `s 86 (5): the thing is a law for s 86` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 86 (5): the thing is a law for s 86` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 86 (5), examples: the thing is a rule of the common law (including equity)` "a common law offence" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 86 (5), examples: the thing is a rule of the common law (including equity)` "a common law rule of practice or procedure" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 86 (5), examples: the thing is a rule of the common law (including equity)` "a right to equitable relief" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 86 (5), examples: the thing is a rule of the common law (including equity)` "a licence" EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 87 (1), (2): repeal of the commencement provision or notice after the law has commenced does not affect the continuing operation of the law.
#ASSERT `s 87 (1): the repeal of the provision providing for the commencement of the law affects the continuing operation of the law` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 87 (1): the repeal of the provision providing for the commencement of the law affects the continuing operation of the law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 87 (2): the repeal of the commencement notice affects the continuing operation of the law` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 87 (2): the repeal of the commencement notice affects the continuing operation of the law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`s 87 (3): s 87 limits any other provision of this chapter`)

-- s 88 (1): the continuing operation of a transitional or validating law is not affected only because the law is repealed.
#ASSERT `s 88 (1), (2): the continuing operation of the law is affected` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 88 (2): (1) does not apply to a law that is transitional or validating only because of modifications it makes to another law.
#ASSERT `s 88 (1), (2): the continuing operation of the law is affected` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 88 (1), (2): the continuing operation of the law is affected` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 88 (1), (2): the continuing operation of the law is affected` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 88 (3): a law declared to be a law to which s 88 applies, and the savings law, do not end only because of repeal.
#ASSERT `s 88 (3): the effect of the declared law or the savings law ends` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 88 (3): the effect of the declared law or the savings law ends` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 88 (4): a declaration may be made whether or not the Act is a law to which subsection (1) applies.
#ASSERT `s 88 (4): a declaration may be made for subsection (3) about the law` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 88 (4): a declaration may be made for subsection (3) about the law` FALSE
-- s 88 (5): a declaration about one law does not imply that, without a declaration, another law is not a law to which the section applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 88 (5): the declaration implies that, without a declaration about it, another law is not a law to which s 88 applies` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 88 (6): s 88 limits any other provision of this chapter`)
-- s 88 (8): the application of s 88 to a law is not displaced only because the law is repealed.
#ASSERT `s 88 (8): the application of s 88 to the law is displaced` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 88 (8): the application of s 88 to the law is displaced` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 88 (9): transitional law: (a) made or expressed to be made for a transitional purpose, or (b) consequential on such a law.
#ASSERT `s 88 (9): the law is a transitional law` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 88 (9): the law is a transitional law` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 88 (9): the law is a transitional law` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 88 (9): validating law: (a) validates something that is or may be invalid, or (b) consequential on such a law.
#ASSERT `s 88 (9): the law is a validating law` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 88 (9): the law is a validating law` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 88 (9): the law is a validating law` FALSE FALSE)

-- s 89 (1) Example: the ABC Act 2005 includes a provision amending the XYZ Act 2000; before it commences the XYZ Act 2000 is repealed (3 March 2026, say);
-- the provision can no longer commence, so the amending law is automatically repealed on the day after, 4 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 89 (1): the day an amending law is automatically repealed` NOTHING (JUST (Date 3 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 4 3 2026)
-- s 89 (7): a repeal under s 89 has effect for all purposes, including the other provisions of this chapter about repeals.
#ASSERT `s 89 (7): a repeal under s 89 has effect for all purposes, including the provisions of this chapter about repeals`
-- s 89 (9): for a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument, the notification day is the day after the day it is made or approved.
#ASSERT `s 89 (9): the notification day of a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument, for s 89 (8)` (Date 3 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 3 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 89 (9): the notification day of a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument, for s 89 (8)` (Date 3 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS Date 10 3 2026
#ASSERT NOT (`s 89 (10): s 89 limits any other provision of this chapter`)
-- s 89 (12): amend does not include modify.
#ASSERT `s 89 (12): the change is an amendment for s 89` `a modification` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 89 (12): the change is an amendment for s 89` `an amendment` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 89 (12): amending law means a law that consists only of provisions of the kinds in (a) to (j); (a) the long title applies for an Act only.
#ASSERT `s 89 (12): the law is an amending law` TRUE (LIST `the Act's long title`, `a preamble or recital`, `a provision about the law's name`, `a provision about the law's commencement`)
#ASSERT `s 89 (12): the law is an amending law` TRUE (LIST `a provision about the purposes of the law or any of its provisions`, `a provision about the effect of notes`, `a provision providing for the amendment or repeal of a law (including a provision identifying the amended or repealed law)`)
#ASSERT `s 89 (12): the law is an amending law` TRUE (LIST `a provision declaring a law to be a law to which section 88 applies`, `a provision about the renumbering of a law`, `a provision authorising or requiring something to be done under chapter 11`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 89 (12): the law is an amending law` FALSE (LIST `the Act's long title`))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 89 (12): the law is an amending law` TRUE (LIST `a provision about the law's name`, `a provision of any other kind`))
-- s 89 (12): amending provision means a provision that only amends or repeals a law, and includes (a) a provision that only identifies the law amended or repealed, (b) a provision that only identifies or groups provisions amended or repealed.
#ASSERT `s 89 (12): the provision is an amending provision` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 89 (12): the provision is an amending provision` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 89 (12): the provision is an amending provision` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 89 (12): the provision is an amending provision` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 89 (12): commencement provision means a provision that only provides for the commencement of the law.
#ASSERT `s 89 (12): the provision is a commencement provision` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 89 (12): the provision is a commencement provision` FALSE)

§§ `Part 9.3: Amendment`

-- s 90: a law and all laws amending it are to be read as one.
#ASSERT `s 90: the law and all laws amending it are to be read as one` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 90: the law and all laws amending it are to be read as one` FALSE)
-- s 91 (1): applies if a law amends another law by inserting a provision and does not exactly specify its position.
#ASSERT `s 91 (1): s 91 applies to the amendment` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 91 (1): s 91 applies to the amendment` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 91 (1): s 91 applies to the amendment` FALSE TRUE)
-- s 91 (2) to (7): the appropriate position of the kinds of inserted provision.
#ASSERT `s 91 (2) to (7): the position of the inserted provision in the amended law` `an inserted chapter, part, division, subdivision, section or subsection` EQUALS `the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position`
#ASSERT `s 91 (2) to (7): the position of the inserted provision in the amended law` `an inserted paragraph` EQUALS `the appropriate alphabetical position`
#ASSERT `s 91 (2) to (7): the position of the inserted provision in the amended law` `an inserted subparagraph` EQUALS `the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position`
#ASSERT `s 91 (2) to (7): the position of the inserted provision in the amended law` `an inserted sub-subparagraph` EQUALS `the appropriate alphabetical position`
#ASSERT `s 91 (2) to (7): the position of the inserted provision in the amended law` `an inserted definition` EQUALS `the appropriate alphabetical position, worked out on a letter-by-letter basis, in a series of definitions`
#ASSERT `s 91 (2) to (7): the position of the inserted provision in the amended law` `a miscellaneous inserted provision` EQUALS `the appropriate position`
#ASSERT `s 91 (8): a reference to a section or subsection is a reference to a corresponding provision of the law` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 91 (8): a reference to a section or subsection is a reference to a corresponding provision of the law` FALSE)
-- s 91 (9): the matters to which regard may be had include the provision number or letter and current legislative drafting practice.
#ASSERT elem "(a) the provision number or letter;" `s 91 (9): the matters to which regard may be had in working out the appropriate position`
#ASSERT elem "(e) current legislative drafting practice." `s 91 (9): the matters to which regard may be had in working out the appropriate position`
-- s 91 (11): insert includes relocate.
#ASSERT `s 91 (11): the thing is an insertion` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 91 (11): the thing is an insertion` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 92 (1): an amendment omitting a word, substituting a word, or inserting a word before or after a particular word is to be made wherever possible.
#ASSERT `s 92 (1): the amendment is to be made wherever possible in the other law` `omitting a word` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 92 (1): the amendment is to be made wherever possible in the other law` `substituting a word for another word` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 92 (1): the amendment is to be made wherever possible in the other law` `inserting a word before or after a particular word` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 92 (1): the amendment is to be made wherever possible in the other law` `another kind of amendment` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 93 (2): a heading forms part of the provision to which it is a heading.
#ASSERT `s 93 (2) to (8): what the material is part of, for the purpose of amending a law` `a heading to a chapter, part, division, subdivision, schedule, dictionary, section or any other provision` FALSE EQUALS `part of the provision it belongs to`
-- s 93 (3), (4): an example or note at the end of a provision is part of it unless expressed to apply only to another provision.
#ASSERT `s 93 (2) to (8): what the material is part of, for the purpose of amending a law` `an example at the end of a provision` FALSE EQUALS `part of the provision it belongs to`
#ASSERT `s 93 (2) to (8): what the material is part of, for the purpose of amending a law` `an example at the end of a provision` TRUE EQUALS `not part of that provision`
#ASSERT `s 93 (2) to (8): what the material is part of, for the purpose of amending a law` `a note at the end of a provision` FALSE EQUALS `part of the provision it belongs to`
#ASSERT `s 93 (2) to (8): what the material is part of, for the purpose of amending a law` `a note at the end of a provision` TRUE EQUALS `not part of that provision`
-- s 93 (5): a note in a law is not, for any other purpose, part of the law.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 93 (5): a note in a law is, for any other purpose, part of the law`)
-- s 93 (6): a penalty at the end of a subsection is part of the subsection unless expressed to apply only to other subsections, when it is part of the section.
#ASSERT `s 93 (2) to (8): what the material is part of, for the purpose of amending a law` `a penalty at the end of a subsection` FALSE EQUALS `part of the provision it belongs to`
#ASSERT `s 93 (2) to (8): what the material is part of, for the purpose of amending a law` `a penalty at the end of a subsection` TRUE EQUALS `part of the section`
-- s 93 (7): a penalty at the end of a section not divided into subsections is part of the section.
#ASSERT `s 93 (2) to (8): what the material is part of, for the purpose of amending a law` `a penalty at the end of a section that is not divided into subsections` FALSE EQUALS `part of the provision it belongs to`
-- s 93 (8): the word and, or or but at the end of a paragraph is part of the provision.
#ASSERT `s 93 (2) to (8): what the material is part of, for the purpose of amending a law` `the word and, or or but, or a similar word, at the end of a paragraph or other provision` FALSE EQUALS `part of the provision it belongs to`
-- s 93 (9): any penalty is disregarded, and for an example any note is disregarded.
#ASSERT `s 93 (9): the thing is disregarded in working out whether the material is at the end of the provision` `an example` `a penalty` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 93 (9): the thing is disregarded in working out whether the material is at the end of the provision` `an example` `a note` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 93 (9): the thing is disregarded in working out whether the material is at the end of the provision` `a note` `a penalty` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 93 (9): the thing is disregarded in working out whether the material is at the end of the provision` `a note` `an example` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 93 (9): the thing is disregarded in working out whether the material is at the end of the provision` `a penalty` `a note` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 93 (10): a reference to a section or subsection is a reference to a corresponding provision of the law` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 93 (10): a reference to a section or subsection is a reference to a corresponding provision of the law` FALSE)

-- s 94 (1): applies if (a) a law authorises or requires the thing, (b) the law is amended, and (c) under the amended law the thing may still be done.
#ASSERT `s 94 (1): s 94 applies to the appointment, instrument, delegation, licence, permit or other thing` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 94 (1): s 94 applies to the appointment, instrument, delegation, licence, permit or other thing` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 94 (1): s 94 applies to the appointment, instrument, delegation, licence, permit or other thing` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 94 (1): s 94 applies to the appointment, instrument, delegation, licence, permit or other thing` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 94 (1) Examples—par (a) (iv): the giving of an approval, consent or permission; the making of a recommendation.
#ASSERT `s 94 (1), examples: the thing is the doing of anything else, under par (a) (iv)` "the giving of an approval, consent or permission" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 94 (1), examples: the thing is the doing of anything else, under par (a) (iv)` "the making of a recommendation" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 94 (1), examples: the thing is the doing of anything else, under par (a) (iv)` "the making of a decision" EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 94 (2): a thing in force immediately before the commencement of the amendment continues to have effect as if made under the amended law.
#ASSERT `s 94 (2): the thing continues to have effect as if it had been made, issued or done under the amended law` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 94 (2): the thing continues to have effect as if it had been made, issued or done under the amended law` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 94 (2): the thing continues to have effect as if it had been made, issued or done under the amended law` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 94 (4): amend includes omit and re-enact in the same law (with or without changes), but does not include omit and re-enact in another law.
#ASSERT `s 94 (4): the change is an amendment for s 94` `an omission and re-enactment in the same law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 94 (4): the change is an amendment for s 94` `an omission and re-enactment in another law` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 94 (4): the change is an amendment for s 94` `a repeal` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 95 (1): if a law is modified by another law, the law operates as modified but the modification does not amend the text of the law.
#ASSERT `s 95 (1): the law operates as modified` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 95 (1): the law operates as modified` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 95 (1): the modification amends the text of the law` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 95 (1): the modification amends the text of the law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 96 (1): applies if a provision of a law is relocated to a different place in the same law or to a different law.
#ASSERT `s 96 (1): s 96 applies to the provision` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96 (1): s 96 applies to the provision` FALSE)
-- s 96 (2): the operation or meaning of the provision is not affected only because of its relocation.
#ASSERT `s 96 (2): the operation or meaning of the provision is affected` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96 (2): the operation or meaning of the provision is affected` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 96 (3): a provision that was to be interpreted in a particular way is interpreted in that way in its new location.
#ASSERT `s 96 (3): the provision is to be interpreted in that way in its new location` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96 (3): the provision is to be interpreted in that way in its new location` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 96 (4): the provision has effect subject to any changes made to, or in relation to, it.
#ASSERT `s 96 (4): the provision has effect subject to the changes` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96 (4): the provision has effect subject to the changes` FALSE)
